The hidden suite is in `packages/core/test/hidden-context-sources-confirmed/`, split into the same seven areas as the public suite. `npx tsc -p tsconfig.test.json` reports no errors. Against the current stubs, all 62 tests fail with `not implemented`.

- **Checked against a working version:** I wrote a straightforward implementation of the spec in the scratchpad, outside the repo. All 128 tests, public and hidden, pass against it.
- **Shortcuts caught:** I then broke that version 14 different ways. Nine of the broken versions still pass the whole public suite, and the hidden suite fails every one of the 14. The nine are:
  - rounding estimates with `toFixed`, so 1260 s gives 0.3 instead of 0.4;
  - never moving a matched root guide (tier 1) ahead of the others;
  - re-trimming text after the cut;
  - splitting the title before lower-casing it (caught with "K", the Kelvin sign, which lower-cases to a plain "k");
  - keeping extra fields on a link because only its key was removed;
  - leaving out the Jira section when the issue has no fields set;
  - removing repeated paths;
  - matching boilerplate stems by prefix, so `changelog.ja.md` would be dropped;
  - dropping documents whose `bytes` is 0 or less.
- **Other gaps covered:**
  - **Ranking:** a matched document never moves ahead of the root README. `./README.md` and `README.ja.md` are not the root README. Paths compare by code point, not `localeCompare`. Nothing is removed or counted before sorting, so the 12-document cut comes after ranking.
  - **Keeping documents:** the shared 48,000-character room shrinks by the kept, trimmed text, not the raw text or `bytes`. A cut can split an emoji in half.
  - **Jira fields:** keys come out in the fixed order whatever order the issue's own keys are in.

Every public scenario, including each boundary and unhappy one, already has a public test. Each hidden test has a comment naming the public test it extends.

One judgement call: a Jira issue with no fields set renders as `Jira fields:\n{}` rather than nothing. The spec only says a *null* Jira source contributes nothing, so I read a non-null issue as always giving its section.

Building the suite also writes compiled output to `packages/core/dist-test/`, which git doesn't show as a change.

62 tests, in 7 files.

Open in the spec: none
